Fig. 2: 
Framework of the proposed instructed speech data pipeline.
It contains three stages: (1) Paired Speech Synthesis, which generates target speeches by combining the anchor speech (providing linguistic content and timbre) with styles from style references;
(2) Quality Evaluation, where target speeches are assessed in terms of word error rate, style similarity, and speaker similarity, and only those that meet the criteria are retained;
and (3) Instruction Design, which employs an LLM to produce editing instructions that link the anchor speech and the target speech.
For each anchor speech, NN style references are sampled, yielding up to NN paired speeches in a single sampling process.
